== 2. Facts for the Conway-Radin-Sadun theorems (exact)
PASS alpha: cos^2 = 1/9, tan^2 = 8 rational (a geodetic angle); tan = +sqrt(8)
PASS alpha: tan is a rational multiple of sqrt2 (square-free part 2)
PASS alpha: (2 cos)^2 = 4/9 is not an integer, so 2 cos is not an algebraic integer and alpha is not a rational multiple of pi
PASS theta_D: cos^2 = 1/5, tan^2 = 4 rational (a geodetic angle); tan = -sqrt(4)
PASS theta_D: tan is a rational multiple of sqrt1 (square-free part 1)
PASS theta_D: (2 cos)^2 = 4/5 is not an integer, so 2 cos is not an algebraic integer and theta_D is not a rational multiple of pi
PASS theta_I: cos^2 = 5/9, tan^2 = 4/5 rational (a geodetic angle); tan = -sqrt(4/5)
PASS theta_I: tan is a rational multiple of sqrt5 (square-free part 5)
PASS theta_I: (2 cos)^2 = 20/9 is not an integer, so 2 cos is not an algebraic integer and theta_I is not a rational multiple of pi
PASS the three tangents lie in three different square classes (sqrt2, 1, sqrt5): by the Splitting Theorem pi, alpha, theta_D, theta_I are linearly independent over Q

